.TH FFF 1 "2024-01-01" "0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fff \- Fucking Fast File Manager (Crystal port)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fff
[\fIDIRECTORY\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
fff is a blazingly fast terminal file manager written in Crystal. It provides a simple and intuitive interface for navigating and managing files using keyboard shortcuts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B DIRECTORY
Start fff in the specified directory instead of the current working directory.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display help information.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Display version information.
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-file-picker
Run as a file picker (for vim/neovim integration).
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.SS Navigation
.TP
.B j, \fB↓\fR
Scroll down
.TP
.B k, \fB↑\fR
Scroll up
.TP
.B h, \fB←\fR
Go to parent directory
.TP
.B l, \fB→\fR, Enter
Go to child directory
.TP
.B g
Go to top
.TP
.B G
Go to bottom
.TP
.B \-
Go to previous directory
.TP
.B ~
Go to home directory
.TP
.B :
Go to directory (type path)
.TP
.B t
Go to trash
.TP
.B e
Refresh current directory
.SS File Operations
.TP
.B y
Mark file for copy
.TP
.B m
Mark file for move
.TP
.B d
Mark file for trash
.TP
.B s
Mark file for symbolic link
.TP
.B b
Mark file for bulk rename
.TP
.B Y
Mark all files for copy
.TP
.B M
Mark all files for move
.TP
.B D
Mark all files for trash
.TP
.B S
Mark all files for symbolic link
.TP
.B B
Mark all files for bulk rename
.TP
.B p
Execute operation
.TP
.B c
Clear all selections
.SS File Management
.TP
.B r
Rename file
.TP
.B n
Create new directory
.TP
.B f
Create new file
.TP
.B x
Show file attributes
.TP
.B X
Toggle executable flag
.TP
.B i
Display image (requires w3m-img)
.SS Search & Shell
.TP
.B /
Search files
.TP
.B !
Spawn shell in current directory
.TP
.B .
Toggle hidden files
.SS Bookmarks
.TP
.B 1-9
Jump to favorite directory
.SS Exit
.TP
.B q
Exit and cd to last directory
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Exit without cd
.SH CONFIGURATION
fff is configured using environment variables:
.SS UI Colors
.TP
.B FFF_COL1
Directory color (0-9, default: 2)
.TP
.B FFF_COL2
Status background color (0-9, default: 7)
.TP
.B FFF_COL3
Selection color (0-9, default: 6)
.TP
.B FFF_COL4
Cursor color (0-9, default: 1)
.TP
.B FFF_COL5
Status foreground color (0-9, default: 0)
.SS File Operations
.TP
.B EDITOR
Text editor (default: vi)
.TP
.B FFF_OPENER
File opener (default: xdg-open)
.TP
.B FFF_STAT_CMD
File attributes command (default: stat)
.SS CD on Exit
.TP
.B FFF_CD_ON_EXIT
Enable cd on exit (0 or 1, default: 1)
.TP
.B FFF_CD_FILE
CD helper file location
.SS Trash
.TP
.B FFF_TRASH
Trash directory
.TP
.B FFF_TRASH_CMD
Trash command (default: mv)
.SS Favorites
.TP
.B FFF_FAV1 \- FFF_FAV9
Favorite directories (keys 1-9)
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start fff in the current directory:
.B fff
.TP
Start fff in a specific directory:
.B fff /home/user/documents
.TP
Use as file picker in vim:
.B fff \-p
.TP
Configure fff in bashrc:
.B export FFF_COL1=4
.B export EDITOR="vim"
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/fff/.fff_d
CD on exit helper file
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/fff/trash/
Default trash directory
